WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.260
Finland orders a halt at two Google sites until environmental reviews finish. This is Omni View Europe,

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:13.320
Episode 15. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. Al Jazeera reports that Finland's environmental

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:20.280
watchdog, the LVV, told 2EK Finland, the firm acting for Google, to pause groundwork in muhose

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:27.520
and kajani. The cutoff is the 23rd of October, 2026, and it lasts until required impact studies are done.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:34.460
In September, Google said it would put 13 billion euros, about $14.6 billion, into

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:36.780
finished digital infrastructure over two years.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:42.980
It called the builds in Mujos, Vala, Kajani, and Hamina, its largest investment in Europe.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:48.560
Investigators are asking whether hundreds of hectares of forest came down without that mandatory

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:49.040
study.

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:54.760
Tommy Muilu, who leads the agency's environment department, said crews had taken out trees,

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:59.740
bodies, stripped topsoil, laid sight roads and storage areas, and changed ditches.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:05.880
Hana Haumeimpa, chair of the Finnish Association for Nature Conservation, told AFP that places

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:09.920
which ought to stay intact, were logged across more than 300 hectares.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:15.700
2EK has until the 14th of October to say how it will proceed, and the agency warned that

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:17.480
enforcement can follow if it does not.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:23.420
Google spokesman Sondre Rononder told AFP the company owned its mistakes, will read the

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:28.640
findings and follow the guidance and plans to plant trees on 130 hectares at moohose.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:33.940
Opposition parties last month asked for a national permit system, citing power shortages

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:35.480
and rising energy prices.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:40.880
Across the region, Norway's minority labor government said on Wednesday, it wants to

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:45.680
pull 608.4 billion Norwegian crowns from the oil fund in 2027.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:52.880
